6. Full Meta-Science Specification
6.1 Meta-Science Schema
The meta-science schema defines the structure of a meta-science dashboard record.

It has the following fields:

dashboard_id. A string. Required.

dashboard_name. A string. Required.

field. A string. Required.

subfield. A string. Optional.

time_period. An object. Required. It contains start_date and end_date.

data_sources. An array of source objects. Required.

metrics. An object. Required. It contains claims_contested, claims_replicated, claims_retracted, claims_superseded, claims_open, claims_total.

trends. An array of trend objects. Required.

comparisons. An array of comparison objects. Optional.

hotspots. An array of hotspot objects. Optional.

cold_spots. An array of cold spot objects. Optional.

funding_impact. An object. Optional. It contains total_funding, funding_per_claim, and funding_distribution.

time_to_resolution. An object. Optional. It contains median_months, mean_months, and distribution.

replication_rate. A number. Optional.

retraction_rate. A number. Optional.

evidence_strength_distribution. An object. Optional. It contains strong, moderate, weak, and inconclusive counts.

provenance. An object. Required.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

Each source object has:

source_id. A string.

source_app. An enum. The values are physics_knowledge_library, replication_tracker, anomaly_register, medical_claim_verifier, psychological_effect_registry, climate_attribution_registry, historical_claim_registry, mathematical_conjecture_registry, claim_lifecycle_tracker, evidence_aggregator, other.

source_record_count. An integer.

source_last_updated. A string in ISO8601 format.

Each trend object has:

trend_id. A string.

metric_name. An enum. The values are claims_contested, claims_replicated, claims_retracted, claims_superseded, claims_open, claims_total, replication_rate, retraction_rate, time_to_resolution, evidence_strength.

trend_period. An object. It contains start_date and end_date.

trend_values. An array of time series values.

trend_direction. An enum. The values are increasing, decreasing, stable, oscillating, unclear.

Each comparison object has:

comparison_id. A string.

compared_field. A string.

compared_metrics. An object. It contains claims_contested, claims_replicated, claims_retracted, claims_superseded, claims_open, claims_total.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each hotspot object has:

hotspot_id. A string.

claim_id. A string.

claim_description. A string.

activity_count. An integer.

activity_type. An enum. The values are replication_attempts, critiques, replications, revisions, funding_events, other.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each cold spot object has:

cold_spot_id. A string.

claim_id. A string.

claim_description. A string.

last_activity_date. A string in ISO8601 format.

months_since_activity. An integer.

notes. A string. Optional.

Each time series value has:

date. A string in ISO8601 format.

value. A number.

